              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log into your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**, follow the steps below to safely access your government services and benefits:\n\n### 1. Go to the Official Login Page\nAlways ensure you are using the official, secure Government of Canada portal:\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Official My Service Canada Account (MSCA) Login Page](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Choose Your Sign-In Method\nOnce on the page, you can choose one of three secure options to log in:\n\n* **Option A: Sign-In Partner (Recommended)**\n  Use your existing online banking credentials from a participating Canadian bank. No financial information is shared with the government; it simply uses your bank's secure login process to verify your identity.\n* **Option B: GCKey**\n  Log in using a government-issued username and password (GCKey) that you have previously created. \n* **Option C: Provincial Sign-In**\n  If you live in **British Columbia** or **Alberta**, you can use your provincial digital identity (such as your *BC Services Card* or *Alberta.ca Account*) to access your MSCA.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Registering for the First Time?\nIf you do not have an account yet, you will need to register. To set up your profile, you will need:\n1. Your **Social Insurance Number (SIN)**.\n2. Your **Personal Access Code (PAC)** (a 4-digit code sent to you via mail or requested online/by phone) or your **EI Access Code**.\n3. To select one of the sign-in methods above (GCKey or Sign-In Partner) to connect to your profile.\n\n---\n\n### Useful Tip: Seamless CRA Linking\nIf you need to access your **Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) My Account** as well as your **My Service Canada Account**, the two are securely linked. Once you log into either account, you can easily click a link to switch over to the other service within the same browser session without having to log in again.\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Security Warning\nService Canada will **never** send you a text message or unsolicited email asking you to click a link to log in, unblock your account, or provide your SIN. Always navigate to **Canada.ca** directly to log in securely.",
